{
  "$comment": "derm setup's policy preset (wave 5, lane W; plans/toolkit_universal_plan.md lane W). `policy` is written to ~/.derm/policy.json as it is; the rest describes it. Command rules (`command`) need contracts/policy.md section 7 in the matchers (lane W's request W-1); until it lands a policy that holds one fails the schema and every call asks, so derm setup refuses to write it.",
  "name": "strict",
  "default": false,
  "summary": "workspace-write with a deny where the plan says strict: force pushes and history rewrites, production deploys, IAM changes, destructive GitHub commands, kubectl apply and delete, terraform apply and destroy. Web searches ask.",
  "boundary": "Every boundary. Under derm's sbx kit (Claude Code, lane T, P4) this file is copied into the VM as it is, and the kit's full access turns every ask into a deny (case 83): there the asks are where work stops, so ordinary work in the project folder is allowed. On the host under srt or as you, an ask is a card (or the agent's own prompt).",
  "readAt": "5 Nov 2026",
  "cli": {
    "git": "2.43.0 (`git push -h`, `git help -a`, run 5 Nov 2026)",
    "gh": "2.89.0 (`gh <group> --help` for pr, issue, repo, release, run, workflow, secret, variable, auth, api; run 5 Nov 2026)",
    "vercel": "65.11.0 (`vercel --help`, `vercel deploy --help`, `env`, `domains`; run 5 Nov 2026; `vc` is the same program, package.json bin)",
    "netlify": "netlify-cli 27.16.2 (dist/commands/deploy/index.js:33-36 `-p, --prod`, `--prod-if-unlocked`; the env:* and sites:* commands; `ntl` is the same program, package.json bin; read, not run)",
    "fly": "flyctl: not installed or read here (GitHub release downloads refused by the workspace's proxy); `fly deploy` and `fly apps destroy` from fly.io's docs index, `flyctl` as fly's other name (I). Not verified",
    "aws": "aws-cli 1.46.2 (pip; the iam service model at awscli/botocore/data/iam/2010-05-08); AWS CLI v2 not read. `aws <service> <operation>`",
    "gcloud": "Google Cloud SDK 570.0.0 (`gcloud --help`, `gcloud iam --help`, `gcloud projects --help`; run 5 Nov 2026)",
    "az": "Azure CLI not installed here; `az role assignment create` from Microsoft Learn, Assign Azure roles using Azure CLI (read 5 Nov 2026); `az ad` from its reference index (I)",
    "docker": "Docker 29.9.2 (`docker run --help`, `docker compose --help`; run 5 Nov 2026)",
    "kubectl": "Kubernetes v1.36 reference, kubectl apply (read 5 Nov 2026); the other verbs from the same reference's index (I). Not installed here",
    "terraform": "Terraform v1.17.x reference, terraform destroy, \"a convenience alias for ... terraform apply -destroy\" (read 5 Nov 2026). Not installed here"
  },
  "gaps": [
    "Shell text with `$`, a backtick, `!`, braces, `~`, a backslash or a glob asks under every preset (step 7b), so in the sbx VM it is denied: the agent must spell commands plainly.",
    "A command reached through a script, a Makefile target, an alias or `find -exec` is not read (policy.md section 7, known limits); a force push by refspec (`git push origin +main`) has no flag to meet.",
    "Hosts: the presets do not ask about curl or wget. The boundary's network rules decide which hosts a chat reaches (srt's allowlist on the host, sbx's policy in the VM).",
    "CI workflow folders (`.github/workflows/`) are not a control path of step 7a yet: lane W's request W-3."
  ],
